# The physical keyboard's layout, one word on a line of its own.
#
# QWERTY, QWERTZ, AZERTY, AZERTY_FR or QWERTZ_DE - the vocabulary legacy used,
# from the com.palm.properties.KEYoBRD token that luna-sysmgr-common's
# DeviceInfo.cpp mapped into PalmSystem.deviceInfo.keyboardType. Reported onward
# by com.webos.service.ime's getKeyboardStatus, which is where WebAppMgr reads it.
#
# It cannot be worked out from the hardware: evdev scancodes are positional, so a
# QWERTZ keyboard and a QWERTY one advertise exactly the same keys, and a USB or
# Bluetooth keyboard carries its layout in the compositor's xkb keymap rather than
# anywhere the input method can see. So it is declared, per device.
#
# One rootfs boots every LuneOS device, so this file is not edited in the image.
# luneos-device-config's 77-hwkeyboard-layout generator bind-mounts a copy over
# it during boot, from deviceinfo_keyboard_layout in the device's adaptation.
#
# All comment means "this device declares nothing", which is the normal case -
# most devices have no physical keyboard. Applications then read keyboardType as
# "Unknown", exactly as they did on hardware legacy had no token for.
